 "text": "Hi, how are you doing? I usually recommend inflating them to half their maximum on first ride after they' new, then every couple of weeks moving them whole way up until they' ready to ride. The tire should feel solid but not springy, and the rim shouldn't feel hot to the touch. Check the side wall for a number, they usually need around six months indoors. Don't go lower than minimum. Keep an eye on them if they stay inflated in rainy weather they need more dry air.",
